Q) You're a data analyst at an e-commerce company. The business wants to understand how customer spending changes from month to month.

Your task is to identify customers whose spending increased compared with the previous month and whose current month's spending exceeded £500.

| OrderID | CustomerID | OrderDate | Amount | Status |
|---:|---:|---|---:|---|
| 1 | 101 | 2026-01-10 | 200 | Completed |
| 2 | 101 | 2026-01-20 | 300 | Completed |
| 3 | 101 | 2026-02-05 | 400 | Completed |
| 4 | 101 | 2026-02-15 | 300 | Completed |
| 5 | 101 | 2026-03-12 | 700 | Completed |
| 6 | 102 | 2026-01-08 | 600 | Completed |
| 7 | 102 | 2026-02-14 | 400 | Completed |
| 8 | 102 | 2026-03-18 | 800 | Completed |
| 9 | 103 | 2026-01-11 | 200 | Completed |
| 10 | 103 | 2026-02-19 | 600 | Completed |
| 11 | 103 | 2026-03-20 | 500 | Completed |
| 12 | 104 | 2026-01-07 | 700 | Cancelled |
| 13 | 104 | 2026-01-15 | 200 | Completed |
| 14 | 104 | 2026-02-10 | 400 | Completed |
| 15 | 104 | 2026-03-15 | 600 | Completed |

Sort the results by CustomerID ascending, then Month ascending.

Write a SQL query to identify customer-month combinations satisfying both conditions:
1. The customer's total spending on completed orders in that month is greater than £500.
2. Their total spending is greater than their spending in the previous calendar month.

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| `CustomerID` | Customer identifier |
| `Month` | Month in `YYYY-MM` format |
| `MonthlySpending` | Total completed-order spending for that month |
| `PreviousMonthSpending` | Total spending in the previous calendar month |

A)
WITH MonthlyTotals AS (
SELECT
    CustomerID,
    DATE_FORMAT(OrderDate, '%Y-%m') AS Month,
    SUM(Amount) AS MonthlySpending
FROM Orders
WHERE Status = 'Completed'
GROUP BY CustomerID, Month
ORDER BY CustomerID, Month
),
MonthlyComparison AS (
    SELECT
        CustomerID,
        Month,
        MonthlySpending,
        LAG(MonthlySpending, 1) OVER (
            PARTITION BY CustomerID
            ORDER BY Month ASC
        ) AS PreviousMonthSpending
    FROM MonthlyTotals
)
SELECT *
FROM MonthlyComparison
WHERE MonthlySpending > 500 AND MonthlySpending > PreviousMonthSpending
ORDER BY CustomerID, Month;
